<p>My interpretations,</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Why isn't the SCP referred to as SCP-2xxx instead of Jacob?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This thing can smash walls even when 'sedated.' So not upsetting it is probably best for continued containment. As to why it wasn't stated plainly&#8212; maybe it was meant to be inferred? That's my best guess.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Finally, the SCP/Jacob mentions fighting terrorists and monsters, much like the MTFs. It shouldn't have that knowledge of the Foundation.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It know it isn't 'normal' and the Foundation are studying it. Logic would suggest other anomalies exist which the Foundation would be interested in.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I also noticed that the age was sixteen, but his mind seemed to be like that of a ten or twelve year old.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>If I read this right, the one doing the talking/thinking is the object connecting through Jacob. Maybe it is 10-12 wherever its from.</p>

